CRASH-03: reject a curve or time series without data, as legacy does

6.0.0 does not crash on a curve or inline time series without data, but
accepts it silently: a storage node runs with an empty storage curve, an
inflow with an empty series. The legacy table check (with the CRASH-03 fix)
rejects such tables with ERROR 171 (curve) or 173 (time series). Add the
same test to the table sequence check in resolve_cross_references(), which
mirrors legacy table_validate(). File-based series are loaded separately
and are not affected.

Apply from the root of a Stormwater-Management-Model checkout at cb3e192b:
    git apply CRASH-03_swmm600.patch

